      "math_academy_id": "q-104579",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $2$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $p(t)=4{t}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by $q(t)=t-1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{q(t)\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)=\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1)+p(2)q(2) \\\\  & =(4{t}^{2}){|}_{0}\\,\\cdot (t\\,-\\,1){|}_{0}+(4{t}^{2}){|}_{1}\\,\\cdot (t\\,-\\,1){|}_{1}+(4{t}^{2}){|}_{2}\\,\\cdot (t\\,-\\,1){|}_{2} \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 0+16\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0+0+16 \\\\  & =16,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),q(t)⟩ & =q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1)+q(2)q(2) \\\\  & =(t\\,-\\,1){|}_{0}\\,\\cdot (t\\,-\\,1){|}_{0}+(t\\,-\\,1){|}_{1}\\,\\cdot (t\\,-\\,1){|}_{1}+(t\\,-\\,1){|}_{2}\\,\\cdot (t\\,-\\,1){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1+0+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2}\\cdot (t-1) \\\\  & =8(t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
